  \"model_expression\": \"P(Ukraine wins) = P(song quality > 70th percentile) × 0.45 + P(song quality 40-70th percentile) × [0.15 + sympathy_boost × war_status] + P(song quality < 40th percentile) × 0.02, where sympathy_boost = 0.25 if war active, 0.12 if recently ended, 0.03 if ended >1yr prior. Adjusted downward by voting_system_changes factor and competitor_strength.\",
  \"confidence\": 0.72,
  \"reasoning\": \"High confidence in historical data (Eurovision results are public and well-documented). Moderate confidence in war trajectory forecasts (inherently uncertain but well-analyzed by military experts). Lower confidence in predicting song quality (unknown until late 2025) and voting reforms (EBU decision-making opaque). The 2022-2023 comparison provides strong empirical basis for sympathy vote decay. Key uncertainty: whether 4 years of war creates compassion fatigue or sustained solidarity. Base rate of 15% for conflict-country wins, but Ukraine's specific circumstances (European war, strong 2022 precedent, cultural soft power) suggest 2-3x multiplier, yielding 30-45% range before song quality adjustment.\"
